WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.639
It's two in the morning.

2
00:00:03.639 --> 00:00:05.738
A discharge notice is in your hand.

3
00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:08.256
A denial letter sits on the kitchen table.

4
00:00:08.957 --> 00:00:12.446
And the system that's supposed to protect the person you love…

5
00:00:12.446 --> 00:00:13.918
has gone completely silent.

6
00:00:15.218 --> 00:00:18.134
For 800,000 Americans living with kidney failure,

7
00:00:18.134 --> 00:00:21.823
and the care partners who carry them, that silence isn't rare.

8
00:00:21.823 --> 00:00:22.597
It's routine.

9
00:00:23.497 --> 00:00:25.059
So we built something to break it.

10
00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.906
This is the Command Center. Every tool.

11
00:00:28.906 --> 00:00:30.174
Every federal contact.

12
00:00:30.174 --> 00:00:32.190
Every complaint pathway. One place.

13
00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:33.112
Completely free.

14
00:00:33.912 --> 00:00:35.535
Start in the Situation Room.

15
00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.751
Describe your crisis.

16
00:00:36.751 --> 00:00:40.692
In under 60 seconds, you get the exact regulation that was violated,

17
00:00:40.692 --> 00:00:44.053
the agency to call, and a complaint letter, ready to file.

18
00:00:44.503 --> 00:00:46.562
Holding a letter written to confuse you?

19
00:00:46.562 --> 00:00:48.622
The Translator puts it in plain English,

20
00:00:48.622 --> 00:00:51.453
and tells you what they're legally required to do next.

21
00:00:51.903 --> 00:00:55.612
Meridian maps your situation to every federal protection that covers it,

22
00:00:55.612 --> 00:00:57.260
and builds your escalation plan.

23
00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:02.262
Narrative Mirror turns what you've lived through into testimony that congressional staff,

24
00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.899
and reporters, can actually use.

25
00:01:04.349 --> 00:01:08.058
Cartography follows the money, the power, and the conflicts of interest,

26
00:01:08.058 --> 00:01:10.325
and shows you exactly where the leverage is.

27
00:01:10.775 --> 00:01:13.146
Two Futures shows the cost of doing nothing.

28
00:01:13.146 --> 00:01:16.973
Authority Strain finds the pressure points that make institutions move.

29
00:01:17.423 --> 00:01:20.751
The Federal Complaint Builder creates a nine letter packet,

30
00:01:20.751 --> 00:01:23.177
pre-cited, and aimed at the right agencies.

31
00:01:23.177 --> 00:01:26.393
Policy Alerts flag every rule change the moment it lands.

32
00:01:26.843 --> 00:01:29.459
Behind it all, live federal intelligence.

33
00:01:29.459 --> 00:01:32.330
An Accountability Atlas with direct contacts.

34
00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:33.926
And a Congress Scorecard,

35
00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:38.137
grading all 535 members on the issues that keep your family alive.

36
00:01:39.037 --> 00:01:42.012
Here's why it works. Vague complaints get archived.

37
00:01:42.012 --> 00:01:43.879
Specific complaints get answers.

38
00:01:44.279 --> 00:01:46.809
Every complaint creates a federal record.

39
00:01:46.809 --> 00:01:48.537
Every record starts a clock.

40
00:01:48.537 --> 00:01:50.388
And every clock they ignore…

41
00:01:50.388 --> 00:01:51.437
becomes evidence.

42
00:01:52.437 --> 00:01:54.077
No pharmaceutical money.

43
00:01:54.077 --> 00:01:57.493
No hospital grants. No insurer on our board. Ever.

44
00:01:58.393 --> 00:02:02.169
Built by patients and care partners, for patients and care partners.

45
00:02:03.069 --> 00:02:04.205
You are not powerless.

46
00:02:04.205 --> 00:02:04.980
You never were.

47
00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:07.488
Welcome to the Command Center.

48
00:02:07.488 --> 00:02:08.513
Let's get to work.
